      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The argument that Big Tech is above the law is a symptom of regulatory capture, not an insurmountable barrier to oversight. The solution isn't to abandon regulation, but to implement modern, technologically sophisticated oversight mechanisms that match the complexity of these firms. Furthermore, the government must actively promote open standards and interoperability, which forces these gatekeepers to compete on merit rather than sheer platform dominance. True oversight requires proactive, structural changes, not just reactive fines.",
      "source": "target",
